DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The llooggiinn__ttookkeenn program implements an X9.9 token card challenge response
     authentication mechanism (see login.conf(5)).  It must be invoked by one
     of the names: llooggiinn__aaccttiivv, llooggiinn__ccrryyppttoo, or llooggiinn__ssnnkk.

     The options are as follows:

     --ss _s_e_r_v_i_c_e
             Specify the service.  Currently only challenge, login, and
             response are supported.

     --vv _n_a_m_e=_v_a_l_u_e
             This option and its value are ignored.

     llooggiinn__ttookkeenn will look up _u_s_e_r in the appropriate database file, depending
     on what name it was called as: _/_e_t_c_/_a_c_t_i_v_._d_b, _/_e_t_c_/_c_r_y_p_t_o_._d_b, or
     _/_e_t_c_/_s_n_k_._d_b.  It then will issue a challenge, and if the user is able to
     correctly respond (by using the appropriate token) the user will be au‐
     thenticated.  The _c_l_a_s_s argument is unused.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/activ.db   data base of information for the ActivCard tokens.

     /etc/crypto.db  data base of information for the CRYPTOCard tokens.

     /etc/snk.db     data base of information for the SNK-004 tokens.

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     Diagnostic messages are logged via syslog(3) with the LOG_AUTH facility.

